  message: "Built and merged in PR #2219 (dev 26f51346b): scripts/publish-scheduled-verdict, a publish-verdict step in both scheduled workflows, README coverage and full-suite badges reading scheduled/*-badge.json on the badges branch. The owner confirmed on 2026-11-17 that the deploy key and the Woodpecker secret badges_deploy_key (cron event) are in place. STAYS OPEN until a scheduled run has published: the SSH push with the real key and the Woodpecker step are not verifiable before the first run after the merge (13:00 UTC 2026-11-17). Close when `git show origin/badges:scheduled/full-suite.json` names that run's own commit and the two badge files exist; if publish-verdict is red, its log holds a one-line reason."  # e125
- op: discuss  # 767f
  at: '2026-11-17T13:53:57Z'  # 767f
  by: agent  # 767f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 767f
  clock: 5  # 767f
  nonce: 767f  # 767f
  message: "FIRST SCHEDULED RUN AFTER THE MERGE, 2026-11-17 13:00 UTC, pipeline 6512 on dev fd5448d1 (ci-debug cron-status at 13:52 UTC): the workflow STARTED, so the secret badges_deploy_key exists and is allowed for the cron event. Every other step passed: git, prepare-git, build-grammars, io-allowlist, allowlist-commands-trace, test-all-packages, self-claims-gate, test-agent-infra, self-tree-validation (the two steps that were red in 6480 are green after PR #2217 and the test-id fix of PR #2223). publish-verdict FAILED (exit 1); its whole log is one line: 'publish-scheduled-verdict: git timed out after 120 s' (ci-debug logs publish-verdict fd5448d1; kept in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/jomid/). origin/badges at 13:52 UTC still holds only coverage.json and last-green-sha.txt (last commit 2026-06-28). SO THE CLOSE CONDITION IS NOT MET and this item stays open. WHAT THE LINE DOES NOT SAY: which git command hung (the message does not name it) or why. The ssh command the script builds has no BatchMode and no ConnectTimeout, so a blocked port 22 from the runner, or ssh waiting for input, would both look like this. NEXT: find out from the runner (a probe of github.com:22 in a PR pipeline needs no secret), make the step fail fast with ssh's own reason, fix, and read the 01:00 UTC run. Until then the scheduled full suite shows FAIL although every test step passed."  # 767f
